{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["Thus says YHWH: 'At about midnight' — כחצות is from חצה, like כעשות from עשה, כעלות המנחה from עלה. That is: when the time of Israel's departure arrives, when the night is halved, I will go out in the midst of Egypt. And at the time of the event it was appropriate to write ויהי בחצי הלילה with a bet — this is according to its plain sense. For when He said it to Moshe before the time of the plague of the firstborn, then it was appropriate to say כחצות, meaning: when that time arrives when the night is halved."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:03.961620617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}